WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.759
Week 2: Greetings and First Contact. greet and take leave introduce yourself and another person choose tú or usted

2
00:00:07.759 --> 00:00:16.201
Form and meaning. Subject pronouns, polite versus familiar address, present-tense ser for identity, and omitted subjects.

3
00:00:16.201 --> 00:00:38.878
Model set. Hola, me llamo Alex. Mucho gusto, señora Rivera. ¿Cómo te llamas? Le presento a mi compañera. Nos vemos mañana; que tenga buen día. Hello, my name is Alex. Nice to meet you, Mrs. Rivera. What is your name? Let me introduce you to my classmate. See you tomorrow; have a good day.

4
00:00:38.878 --> 00:00:49.008
Contrastive practice. Change the person, time, number, or level of formality in each model. Preserve the communicative purpose while the grammar changes.

5
00:00:49.008 --> 00:01:01.762
Production check. Say one original sentence for each function: greet and take leave; introduce yourself and another person; choose tú or usted. Then write it and compare the spoken and written forms.

6
00:01:01.762 --> 00:01:25.121
Model language. Hola, me llamo Alex. — Hello, my name is Alex. Mucho gusto, señora Rivera. — Nice to meet you, Mrs. Rivera. ¿Cómo te llamas? — What is your name? Le presento a mi compañera. — Let me introduce you to my classmate. Nos vemos mañana; que tenga buen día. — See you tomorrow; have a good day.

7
00:01:25.121 --> 00:01:34.870
Check your readiness. Explain the core idea. Produce an original example. Complete the section assessment at 85% or higher.
